  "name": "Question 20",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14187307/assets/8d861b8d473ffe6b56105636da5ea51bb5fd33685b454800d376616b5cf2e311.png)\n\nThe password of Carla's computer has ten characters. Each character is a number among $1$ and $9.$ The ratio of odd numbers to even numbers is shown in the diagram above. How many even numbers her password has?",
  "worked_solution": "The tape diagram shows $2$ boxes corresponding to odd numbers, and $3$ boxes corresponding to even numbers. Therefore, the ratio of odd to even in the password is $2:3.$\n\nWe are told that the password has $10$ characters. The tape diagram has $2+3=5$ boxes in total. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $10÷5=2$ numbers.\n\nNow, we fill the number $2$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14187307/assets/7dc4dedfb2550e65ad1146b5103fc00ac1cc0d447258d336602df4b7be93a658.png)\n\nSince there are $3$ boxes corresponding to even numbers, and each box represents $2$ numbers, the number of even numbers must be:\n\n$$\n3\\times 2=6.\n$$\n\nSo, Carla's password has $6$ even numbers.",
